<item>
            <title>[LU-20525] Lustre utilities interactive mode defects</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20525</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When lnetctl , lctl or lfs utilities are invoked in interactive mode, the first compound command works correctly however the subsequent commands fail():&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;[root@rocky96 wc-master]# ./lnet/utils/lnetctl 
&amp;gt; net show
net:
-     net type: lo
      local NI(s):
      -     nid: 0@lo
            status: up
-     net type: tcp
      local NI(s):
      -     nid: 192.168.50.90@tcp
            status: up
            interfaces:
                  0: eth1
&amp;gt; net show
usage: lt-lnetctl [COMMAND] [OPTIONS]... [ARGS]
Without any parameters, interactive mode is invoked
Try &apos;lt-lnetctl help &amp;lt;COMMAND&amp;gt;&apos;, or &apos;lt-lnetctl --list-commands&apos; for a list of commands.
&amp;gt; net show --verbose
usage: lt-lnetctl [COMMAND] [OPTIONS]... [ARGS]
Without any parameters, interactive mode is invoked
Try &apos;lt-lnetctl help &amp;lt;COMMAND&amp;gt;&apos;, or &apos;lt-lnetctl --list-commands&apos; for a list of commands.
&amp;gt; add
missing mandatory parameters in NI config: &apos;network&apos;
&amp;gt; 
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;the happens with lctl command, for example, nodemap info:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;[root@rocky96 wc-master]# ./lustre/utils/lctl
&amp;gt; nodemap info
nodemap.active=0
nodemap.default.admin_nodemap=0
nodemap.default.audit_mode=1
nodemap.default.banlist=[]
nodemap.default.child_raise_privileges=none
nodemap.default.deny_mount=0
nodemap.default.deny_unknown=0
nodemap.default.dt_stats=
...
nodemap.default.rbac=file_perms,dne_ops,quota_ops,byfid_ops,chlg_ops,fscrypt_admin,server_upcall,ignore_root_prjquota,hsm_ops,pool_quota_ops,lqa_quota_ops,projid_set,foreign_ops
nodemap.default.readonly_mount=0
nodemap.default.squash_gid=65534
nodemap.default.squash_projid=65534
nodemap.default.squash_uid=65534
nodemap.default.trusted_nodemap=0
&amp;gt; nodemap info
usage: lt-lctl nodemap [COMMAND] [OPTIONS]... [ARGS]
Without any parameters, interactive mode is invoked
Try &apos;lt-lctl nodemap help &amp;lt;COMMAND&amp;gt;&apos;, or &apos;lt-lctl nodemap --list-commands&apos; for a list of commands.
&amp;gt; 

&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;i.e. it is a common problem for the lustre interactive utilities.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
